  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Temporary Support and Assistance to Sensitive Myanmar Nationals Transiting through the Republic of Korea to the United States</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A severe crisis in Myanmar has resulted in increased mobility and displacement both within the country and into neighbouring countries, including Thailand. The ongoing COVID-19 pandemic exacerbates the problem and risks increasing the vulnerability of the affected populations. The Bureau of Democracy, Human Rights and Labor (DRL) agreed with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs (MOFA) of the Republic of Korea (ROK) to allow several selected vulnerable Myanmar nationals evacuated from Thailand to stay in the transit area of the Incheon International Airport until their departure following the completion of their parole processing for their entry to the US. IOM support and assistance includes providing accommodation, meals and necessary personal protective equipment to the beneficiaries at the Incheon Airport during the whole period of stay, as well as facilitating the transfer of necessary travel documentation, meeting and escorting the beneficiary upon their arrival and prior to their departure from the Incheon airport.</narrative>
  </description>
